use std
into grow_look.amni

A picture tool for the `grow` library; imports math, os, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes, gfx.scene3d, grow.grow and grow.forms. Already provided and never defined here: `grow::make`, `grow::KINDS`, `grow::glb_bytes`, `gltf::load_bytes(data, dir) int`, `shapes::plane(half, material) int`, `shapes::material(rgb, metallic, roughness)`, `linalg::compose(t, r, s)`, `linalg::qaxis(axis, angle)`, `linalg::quat_identity()`, `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::flush()`, `gfx::save_png(target, path)`, `s3d::init(w, h)`, `s3d::add(asset) int`, `s3d::place(item, matrix)`, `s3d::render(target)`, `s3d::atmosphere(to_sun float3, power, haze, clouds)` and the settings `s3d::temporal`, `s3d::ssr_on`, `s3d::ssgi_on`, `s3d::gi_on`, `s3d::look.bloom`, `s3d::sun.shadows`, `s3d::sun.shadow_far`, `s3d::view.eye`, `s3d::view.target`, `s3d::view.up`, `s3d::view.fov_y`, `s3d::view.near` and `s3d::view.far` (float3 and f32 fields). The picture is 1280 by 720.

`grown(kind, s, size) int` makes that kind with that seed and size, writes it with `glb_bytes` and returns `gltf::load_bytes` of those bytes with dir "".

`put(asset, x, z, turn)` adds the asset to the scene and places it at (x, 0, z) turned by turn radians about the Y axis, scale 1.

`shoot(name)` renders twice into the render target (flushing after each) and saves it as a PNG named name plus ".png" inside the output folder.

`main()`: the first argument after the program name (index 1 of `args()`) is the output folder (print "grow_look: needs an output folder" and stop without one). Open headless at the picture size, or print "grow_look: skipped" and stop. Set up the scene: init, temporal 0, no SSR, SSGI or GI, bloom 0, sun shadows on with shadow_far 60, atmosphere with the sun at 40 degrees up (direction (0.6 cos e, sin e, 0.8 cos e)) power 3.5, haze 1, clouds 0.3; a ground `plane` of half size 200 with a warm soil material (0.30, 0.24, 0.17), metallic 0, roughness 0.95. Shot "lineup": all fourteen kinds in `KINDS` order at seed 7177 and size 1, seven per row, rows at z 0 and z -1.7, x from -5.1 in steps of 1.7, camera eye (0, 2.7, 7), target (0, 0.4, -0.8), up (0, 1, 0), fov_y 0.77, near 0.05, far 300; print each kind with its asset id. Then shot "glade": for seeds 1 to 7 of the same kinds placed on a second patch far away (centered at x 100), a tree of size 4.7 at (100, -3), two pines of size 3.7 at (97, -7) and (104, -6), a bush of 1.2 at (102, -1), three rocks of 0.7 to 1.1, five ferns of 0.7, seven flowers of 0.47, five mushrooms of 0.17, seventeen tufts of 0.27 and two mossy rocks of 0.7 scattered within 4 m of (100, 0) by a fixed seed 7177 (using `grow::seed` and `grow::range` for positions and turns), camera eye (100, 1.7, 5.7), target (100, 1.1, -2), same up and fov. Print "grow_look: ok".
